<section class="evidence-band signal-chain-dossier" aria-labelledby="bench-order-heading">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>MINIMUM BENCH ORDER</p>
      <h2 id="bench-order-heading">INSPECT. IDENTIFY. ISOLATE. THEN APPLY POWER.</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="progression-list">
      <li class="active">
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Bench Surface</h3>
        <p>Move the board from its plastic storage tray to a clean cardboard motherboard box or another rigid nonconductive surface. Never power atop an antistatic bag.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>CPU + Cooling</h3>
        <p>Keep the confirmed 5930K seated and the socket latched. Fit a compatible LGA2011-v3 air cooler with fresh thermal paste.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>One Memory Module</h3>
        <p>Install one known-good non-ECC unbuffered DDR4 UDIMM at JEDEC speed in DIMM1. Eight slots do not mean eight installed modules.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Power + Display</h3>
        <p>Use the non-modular Thermaltake 600 W only after its model label, age, leads, and condition are cleared. Connect its fixed 24-pin ATX, native CPU/EPS 8-pin, and GPU PCIe lead to the air-cooled GTX 1060 6 GB.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>05</span>
        <h3>Clear + Record</h3>
        <p>Disconnect incoming power, clear CMOS, use the onboard power control, and capture the two-digit debug code and all fan or temperature behavior.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>06</span>
        <h3>Stop Boundary</h3>
        <p>Exclude drives, M.2, Wi-Fi, networking, pumps, liquid blocks, BIOS flashing, overclocking, and permanent installation. Never power the waterblocked GTX 780 dry. Preserve the unverified AX1500i. Stop for smoke, arcing, sharp electrical odor, or abnormal heat.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

